ll furry things are kind" implies that if something is furry, it must be kind.\n   - "If Harry is young then Harry is cold" implies that if Harry is young, he must be cold.\n   - "If something is young and cold then it is furry" implies that if something is young and cold, it must be furry.\n\n3. **Determine Harry\'s status:**.\n   - Harry is green.\n   - Harry is big.\n   - Therefore, Harry is young (from "All big, green things are young" and "Big things are young").\n   - Harry is not red (from "If something is kind then it is not red" and "All furry things are kind").\n\n4. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Since Harry is not red, the statement "Harry is red" is false.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
