 fits our deductions: A is a knight, B is a knave, and C can be a spy.\n\nB) A is a knave, B is a knight, C is a spy\n   - This option is incorrect because A cannot be a knave (A is a knight).\n\nC) A is a spy, B is a knight, C is a spy\n   - This option is incorrect because A cannot be a spy (A is a knight).\n\nD) A is a spy, B is a knave, C is a spy\n   - This option is incorrect because A cannot be a spy (A is a knight).\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:\nA) A is a knight, B is a knave, C is a spy.\n</think>\n<answer>A) A is a knight, B is a knave, C is a spy</answer>",
