asses: \\( |G_g| = 5 \\)\n   - Number of boys wearing glasses: \\( |B_g| = 5 \\)\n\n3. **Use the principle of inclusion-exclusion for the total number of students:**\n   \\[\n   |G \\cup B| = |G| + |B| - |G \\cap B|\n   \\]\n   Since \\( G \\cap B = \\emptyset \\):\n   \\[\n   30 = 18 + 12 - 0\n   \\]\n   This confirms the total number of students is correctly given.\n\n4. **Verify the number of students wearing glasses:**\n   \\[\n   |G_g| + |B_g| = 5 + 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   This matches the given information.\n\n5. **Determine the number of students wearing glasses who are girls:**\n   - We are given that the number of girls wearing glasses is 5.\n\nThus, the number of students wearing glasses and are girls is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{A}\n\\]\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe number of students wearing glasses and are girls is 5, which matches the given information directly. Therefore, the correct option is:\nA) 5\n</answer>",
