ve is furry.").\n   - Therefore, Dave is quiet.\n\n6. **If Dave is Furry, Then Dave is Nice:**.\n   - If Dave is furry, then Dave is nice.\n   - Dave is furry (from the context: "Dave is furry.").\n   - Therefore, Dave is nice.\n\n7. **All Nice Things Are Furry:**.\n   - If something is nice, then it is furry.\n   - Dave is nice (from step 6).\n   - Therefore, Dave is furry.\n\n8. **All Smart Things Are Nice:**.\n   - If something is smart, then it is nice.\n   - Gary is smart (from the context: "Gary is smart.").\n   - Therefore, Gary is nice.\n   - Since Dave is nice (from step 6), Dave is not smart.\n\n9. **Quiet Things Are Red:**.\n   - If something is quiet, then it is red.\n   - Dave is quiet (from step 1).\n   - Therefore, Dave is red.\n\n10. **Red Things Are Green:**.\n    - If something is red, then it is green.\n    - Dave is red (from step 9).\n    - Therefore, Dave is green.\n\nFrom the above logical deductions, we can conclude that Dave is nice. Therefore, the statement "Dave is not nice" is false.\n\n**Final Answer: B) False**.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
