y. Since Fiona is furry, she cannot be red and big.\n- From point 15, if something is furry and smart, it is big. Since Fiona is furry, she could be big and smart.\n\nGiven that Fiona is furry and young, and we know that young things are not red, we need to check if she can be smart:.\n\n- From point 12, smart things are furry. Since Fiona is furry, she could be smart.\n- From point 13, if Charlie is red, he is kind. However, we don\'t have any information about Fiona being red.\n- From point 15, if something is furry and smart, it is big. Since Fiona is furry, she could be big and smart.\n\nSince we don\'t have any direct information that explicitly states Fiona is not smart, and we can\'t definitively rule out the possibility that she is smart based on the given information, the statement "Fiona is not smart" remains unknown.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
