 be green. We need to see if there\'s any contradiction or additional information that would make Erin green.\n   - If Erin were green, she would need to be rough (since green, smart people are rough). However, we don\'t have any information that directly states Erin is rough.\n   - Therefore, Erin being green is not confirmed by the given information.\n\n5. **Checking Erin\'s Roughness:**.\n   - Since Erin is furry, she is smart (as per the given information).\n   - We need to see if there\'s any contradiction or additional information that would make Erin rough.\n   - There is no information that directly states Erin is rough or not rough.\n\n6. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Erin is cold and furry.\n   - Since Erin is furry, she is smart.\n   - There is no information that contradicts Erin being smart.\n\nTherefore, based on the given context, the statement "Erin is smart" is true.\n\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
