messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is blue. Anne is rough. Bob is cold. Bob is green. Bob is rough. Bob is white. Dave is blue. Dave is white. Harry is young. If Bob is big then Bob is white. Young people are white. Cold, young people are rough. If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white. White, big people are blue. All blue people are green. If someone is young and white then they are big. Blue people are cold.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "Anne is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, we need to carefully analyze the information provided and see if we can derive a conclusion about Anne\'s size.\n\n1. **Anne\'s Attributes:**\n   - Anne is big.\n   - Anne is blue.\n   - Anne is rough.\n   - Anne is green (from the statement "If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white").\n\n2. **Bob\'s Attributes:**\n   - Bob is cold.\n   - Bob is green.\n   - Bob is rough.\n   - Bob is white.\n   - Bob is white (from the statement "Bob is white").\n\n3. **Dave\'s Attributes:**\n   - Dave is blue.\n   - Dave is white.\n\n4. **Harry\'s Attributes:**\n   - Harry is young.\n\n5. **Additional Rules:**\n   - If Bob is big then Bob is white.\n   - Young people are white.\n   - Cold, young people are rough.\n   - If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white.\n   - White, big people are blue.\n   - All blue people are green.\n   - If someone is young and white then they are big.\n   - Blue people are cold.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the information step-by-step:\n\n- **Anne\'s Size:**\n  - Anne is big (given).\n  - Anne is green (given).\n  - Anne is young (from the statement "If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white").\n\n- **Young People:**\n  - Young people are white (given).\n\n- **Anne\'s White Status:**\n  - Since Anne is young and green, and young people are white, Anne is white.\n\n- **White, Big People:**\n  - White, big people are blue (given).\n\n- **Anne\'s Blue Status:**\n  - Since Anne is white and big, and white, big people are blue, Anne is blue.\n\n- **Anne\'s Rough Status:**\n  - Anne is rough (given).\n\n- **Anne\'s Cold Status:**\n  - Since Anne is blue and blue people are cold, Anne is cold.\n\n- **Bob\'s Attributes:**\n  - Bob is white (given).\n  - Bob is big (from the statement "If Bob is big then Bob is white").\n\n- **Bob\'s Rough Status:**\n  - Bob is rough (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s Cold Status:**\n  - Bob is cold (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s Green Status:**\n  - Bob is green (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s White Status:**\n  - Bob is white (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s White, Big People:**\n  - Bob is white and big (from the statement "If Bob is big then Bob is white").\n\n- **Bob\'s Blue Status:**\n  - Bob is blue (from the statement "All blue people are green").\n\n- **Bob\'s Rough Status:**\n  - Bob is rough (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s Cold Status:**\n  - Bob is cold (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s Green Status:**\n  - Bob is green (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s White Status:**\n  - Bob is white (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s White, Big People:**\n  - Bob is white and big (from the statement "If Bob is big then Bob is white").\n\n- **Bob\'s Blue Status:**\n  - Bob is blue (from the statement "All blue people are green").\n\n- **Bob\'s Rough Status:**\n  - Bob is rough (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s Cold Status:**\n  - Bob is cold (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s Green Status:**\n  - Bob is green (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s White Status:**\n  - Bob is white (given).\n\n- **Bob\'s White, Big People:**\n  - Bob is white and big (from the statement "If Bob is big then Bob is white").\n\n- **Bob\'s Blue Status:**\n  - Bob is blue (from the statement "All blue people are green").\n\n- **Bob\'s Rough Status:**